{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-sql-13b/sub-exists-vs-in-null",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-SQL-1",
    "SQL-SUB-02",
    "SQL-SUB-04"
  ],
  "description": "With Null keys on both sides (JA.a, JB.b), do EXISTS, NOT EXISTS, IN and NOT IN over the same correlated test give the same JA rows; what does the projected EXISTS and NOT EXISTS give; and what do EXISTS and NOT EXISTS give over an empty table (CZ), over a child selecting only Null, over a multi-column child, with a trailing OR, and when the subquery has no parentheses? Runs on a fresh copy of r-sql-13b-main (ACCDB) opened read-only through ACE DAO; each text is opened as a snapshot with Database.OpenRecordset, Fields Name/Type/Size are read before the first row, then every row's Field values to EOF (each MoveNext captured), then Close and DBEngine.Errors.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
